      "writtenOn": "2025-12-05T02:08:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks. What I actually had in mind: perhaps we wouldn\u0027t need hypercalls for those registers, we could just let the host transparently set them, via emulated registers, in direct_access_iommu_mmio(), and looks like we are actually already doing that?\n\nAnyway, tl;dr now I see in VT-d spec section 7.4.1 that to actually enable PRQ we\u0027d need, among other things, to enable Page Request Enable (PRE) bit in the context entry (context_set_sm_pre()) and I see we don\u0027t do that in pKVM. So as a matter of fact, we don\u0027t support PRQ, for good or bad, so it makes sense to disable its usage by the host driver.",
      "parentUuid": "d60a5016_483cb2c9",
      "revId": "c51ca3b4c680cd22586004879e5fb44db44d1044",
